    // FILE: D:\GOG\Battle Brothers\!Downloads\bbros\bin\comparer\original_current\scripts\contracts\contracts\raze_attached_location_contract.nut
    {
        en = "Raze Location"
        es = "Arrasar ubicación"
    }
    {
        // "Raze " + this.Flags.get("DestinationName") + " near " + this.Flags.get("SettlementName")
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "Raze <this.Flags.get(DestinationName)> near <this.Flags.get(SettlementName)>"
        es = "Arrasar <this.Flags.get(DestinationName)> cerca de <this.Flags.get(SettlementName)>"
    }
    {
        en = "Done"
        es = ""
    }
    {
        // Text = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_61.png[/img]{%employer% throws back his silken sleeves and cracks his knuckles.%SPEECH_ON%I hope I can entrust you with a most delicate matter as my family cannot be connected to what I am about to tell you.%SPEECH_OFF%You nod as though a sellsword is often asked to keep a secret. The man continues.%SPEECH_ON%The town of %settlementname% is too weak to protect itself and the people are clamoring for protection from brigands. We, the house of %noblehousename%, are the only ones who can truly offer the safety they seek. Unfortunately, the local council is too blind to see this. They are convinced they can guard their people themselves. Let us prove them wrong.\n\n I want you to burn the %location% close to %settlementname% to the ground and kill the peasantry there. Make it look like brigands did it. I\'m sure you are familiar with their work. Now...%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% leans in close.%SPEECH_ON%...let me be very clear and I need you to listen very closely. There must be no survivors that could tell who really attacked them. None! Understand? Good. Return to me once the deed is done.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% stares at a pile of scrolls before angrily swiping them off his table in a flurry of papery madness.%SPEECH_ON%The councilmen of %settlementname% think they can protect their little town from brigands, but I know they can\'t. I know they need my protection! And I offered it at such a reasonable price...%SPEECH_OFF%He calms down just long enough to glance at you.%SPEECH_ON%I got it. I know what to do. You... you\'re familiar with a brigand\'s doings, yes? Of course. So how about you... go to %location% outside of %settlementname% and... do what a brigand what do. Of course, make it actually look like a brigands doing... after that, surely the town will contract me to protect them! And then they will be safe!%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% has his hands tented, the tips of them pressed against his forehead. He lets out a long sigh.%SPEECH_ON%I\'ve tried to deal with these people of %settlementname% for quite some years now, but I\'m beginning to think I\'ll have to take drastic measures to get what I want. The council there won\'t pay me to protect their village because they think they can do it themselves. They say that they\'ve been safe from harm for quite some time now. So what if... they weren\'t? What if you were to go in there, dressed as a brigand of course, and teach them that without the aid of %noblehousename% nobody is safe! Of course, you mustn\'t tell anyone of our little talk here... What say you, mercenary?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%\'s staring out the window as you settle into a seat.%SPEECH_ON%Stand up, sellsword. I don\'t like to whisper down, it gets me to raise my voice and with what I\'m about to tell you I don\'t think I want to be doing that.%SPEECH_OFF%You stand up and lend your ear.%SPEECH_ON%%settlementname% has refused my offer of protection. They\'ve decided to go it alone. Not only are they not paying %noblehousename%, but they\'re besmirching our name. If this village refuses our protection, what will others do? I need you to take the \'part\' of a brigand, go there, and teach them what it is to go in this world without %noblehousename% by your side! Of course, discretion is of the utmost importance. Nothing I\'ve said here must leave this room.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%\'s rubbing an apple raw, peeling back the rind with the grit of his thumb.%SPEECH_ON%My father used to tell me, if you don\'t have a name that raises respect just by its sound, then you have no name at all. Unfortunately, %settlementname% does not respect the name of %noblehousename%. They\'ve refused my offers of protection and have insulted my family. I want you to pay them back for this. I want you to go there, not as mercenaries but as brigands, and show them what happens in a world without %noblehousename%\'s protection. Of course, you must be thorough, sellsword. You mustn\'t tell anyone of what we say in this here room.%SPEECH_OFF%}",
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_61.png[/img]\x7b%employer% throws back his silken sleeves and cracks his knuckles.%SPEECH_ON%I hope I can entrust you with a most delicate matter as my family cannot be connected to what I am about to tell you.%SPEECH_OFF%You nod as though a sellsword is often asked to keep a secret. The man continues.%SPEECH_ON%The town of %settlementname% is too weak to protect itself and the people are clamoring for protection from brigands. We, the house of %noblehousename%, are the only ones who can truly offer the safety they seek. Unfortunately, the local council is too blind to see this. They are convinced they can guard their people themselves. Let us prove them wrong.\n\n I want you to burn the %location% close to %settlementname% to the ground and kill the peasantry there. Make it look like brigands did it. I'm sure you are familiar with their work. Now...%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% leans in close.%SPEECH_ON%...let me be very clear and I need you to listen very closely. There must be no survivors that could tell who really attacked them. None! Understand? Good. Return to me once the deed is done.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% stares at a pile of scrolls before angrily swiping them off his table in a flurry of papery madness.%SPEECH_ON%The councilmen of %settlementname% think they can protect their little town from brigands, but I know they can't. I know they need my protection! And I offered it at such a reasonable price...%SPEECH_OFF%He calms down just long enough to glance at you.%SPEECH_ON%I got it. I know what to do. You... you're familiar with a brigand's doings, yes? Of course. So how about you... go to %location% outside of %settlementname% and... do what a brigand what do. Of course, make it actually look like a brigands doing... after that, surely the town will contract me to protect them! And then they will be safe!%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% has his hands tented, the tips of them pressed against his forehead. He lets out a long sigh.%SPEECH_ON%I've tried to deal with these people of %settlementname% for quite some years now, but I'm beginning to think I'll have to take drastic measures to get what I want. The council there won't pay me to protect their village because they think they can do it themselves. They say that they've been safe from harm for quite some time now. So what if... they weren't? What if you were to go in there, dressed as a brigand of course, and teach them that without the aid of %noblehousename% nobody is safe! Of course, you mustn't tell anyone of our little talk here... What say you, mercenary?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%'s staring out the window as you settle into a seat.%SPEECH_ON%Stand up, sellsword. I don't like to whisper down, it gets me to raise my voice and with what I'm about to tell you I don't think I want to be doing that.%SPEECH_OFF%You stand up and lend your ear.%SPEECH_ON%%settlementname% has refused my offer of protection. They've decided to go it alone. Not only are they not paying %noblehousename%, but they're besmirching our name. If this village refuses our protection, what will others do? I need you to take the 'part' of a brigand, go there, and teach them what it is to go in this world without %noblehousename% by your side! Of course, discretion is of the utmost importance. Nothing I've said here must leave this room.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer%'s rubbing an apple raw, peeling back the rind with the grit of his thumb.%SPEECH_ON%My father used to tell me, if you don't have a name that raises respect just by its sound, then you have no name at all. Unfortunately, %settlementname% does not respect the name of %noblehousename%. They've refused my offers of protection and have insulted my family. I want you to pay them back for this. I want you to go there, not as mercenaries but as brigands, and show them what happens in a world without %noblehousename%'s protection. Of course, you must be thorough, sellsword. You mustn't tell anyone of what we say in this here room.%SPEECH_OFF%\x7d"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_61.png[/img]\x7b%employer% se remanga las mangas de seda y cruje los nudillos. %SPEECH_ON%Espero poder confiarle un asunto muy delicado, ya que mi familia no debe estar relacionada con lo que estoy a punto de decirle.%SPEECH_OFF%Asientes como si a menudo se le pidiera a un mercenario que guardara un secreto. El hombre continúa. %SPEECH_ON%La ciudad de %settlementname% es demasiado débil para protegerse a sí misma y la gente está clamando por protección contra bandidos. Nosotros, la %noblehousename%, somos los únicos que realmente podemos ofrecer la seguridad que buscan. Desafortunadamente, el consejo local es demasiado ciego para ver esto. Están convencidos de que pueden proteger a su gente por sí mismos. Permita que les demostremos que están equivocados.\n\nQuiero que quemes el %location% cerca de %settlementname% hasta los cimientos y mates a la plebe allí. Haz que parezca que los bandidos lo hicieron. Estoy seguro de que estás familiarizado con ese trabajo. Ahora... %SPEECH_OFF% %employer% se acerca mucho.%SPEECH_ON%...permíteme ser muy claro y necesito que escuches muy atentamente. No debe haber supervivientes que puedan decir quiénes realmente los atacaron. ¡Ninguno! ¿Entendido? Bien. Regresa a mí una vez que se haya hecho el trabajo.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% mira un montón de pergaminos antes de apartarlos en un frenesí de papel.%SPEECH_ON%Los concejales de %settlementname% creen que pueden proteger su pequeña ciudad de los bandidos, pero yo sé que no pueden. ¡Sé que necesitan mi protección! Y la ofrecí a un precio tan razonable...%SPEECH_OFF%Se calma solo el tiempo suficiente para mirarte.%SPEECH_ON%Lo tengo. Sé qué hacer. Tú... conoces las acciones de un bandido, ¿verdad? Por supuesto. Entonces, ¿qué tal si... vas a %location% cerca de %settlementname% y... haces lo que haría un bandido? Por supuesto, asegúrate de que realmente parezca que lo hicieron los bandidos... después de eso, ¡seguro que la ciudad me contratará para protegerlos! ¡Y luego estarán a salvo!%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% tiene las manos entrelazadas, las puntas de los dedos presionadas contra su frente. Deja escapar un largo suspiro. %SPEECH_ON%He intentado tratar con la gente de %settlementname% durante bastante tiempo, pero empiezo a pensar que tendré que tomar medidas drásticas para conseguir lo que quiero. El consejo allí no me pagará por proteger su pueblo porque creen que pueden hacerlo por sí mismos. Dicen que han estado a salvo de daños durante bastante tiempo. Entonces, ¿qué pasa si... no lo han estado? ¿Qué pasaría si fueras allí, vestido como un bandido, por supuesto, y les enseñaras que sin la ayuda de la %noblehousename% nadie está a salvo? Por supuesto, no debes contarle a nadie nuestra pequeña charla aquí... ¿Qué dices, mercenario?%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% está mirando por la ventana mientras tomas asiento. %SPEECH_ON%Levántate, espadachín. No me gusta susurrar, me hace elevar la voz y con lo que estoy a punto de decir, no creo que quiera hacer eso.%SPEECH_OFF%Te levantas y prestas atención. %SPEECH_ON%El consejo de %settlementname% ha rechazado mi oferta de protección. Han decidido ir por su cuenta. No solo no están pagando a la %noblehousename%, sino que están difamando nuestro nombre. Si este pueblo rechaza nuestra protección, ¿qué harán los demás? Necesito que asumas el 'papel' de un bandido, vayas allí y les enseñes lo que significa vivir en este mundo sin la %noblehousename% a su lado. Por supuesto, la discreción es de la máxima importancia. Nada de lo que he dicho aquí debe salir de esta habitación.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% pela una manzana a mano, pelando la piel con el pulgar. %SPEECH_ON%Mi padre solía decirme que si no tienes un nombre que genere respeto solo por su sonido, entonces no tienes nombre en absoluto... Desafortunadamente, %settlementname% no respeta a la %noblehousename%. Han rechazado mis ofertas de protección e insultado a mi familia. Quiero que les devuelvas esto. Quiero que vayais allí, no como mercenarios, sino como bandidos, y les muestres lo que sucede en un mundo sin la protección de la %noblehousename%. Por supuesto, debes ser minucioso, mercenario. No debes contarle a nadie lo que decimos en esta sala.%SPEECH_OFF%\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "\x7bLet's talk money. | How many crowns are we talking about? | What will the pay be? | For the right price, everything can be done.\x7d"
        es = "\x7bHablemos de dinero. | ¿De cuántas coronas estamos hablando? | ¿Cuánto será la paga? | Por el precio justo, todo puede ser hecho...\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "\x7bThat's not our line of work. | That's not for the %companyname%.\x7d"
        es = "\x7bEsa no es nuestro tipo de trabajo. | Esto no es para %companyname%. | Somos mercenarios, no bandidos.\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_16.png[/img]\x7bYou reach the %location%. Peasants are out and about just as you figured. This will be like spearing fish in a barrel. Now the only question is: how do you want to approach? | %location% is a little more serene than you thought it'd be. A few peasants mosey about, chucking sickles and hoes around as they banter about this or that. You hear them barking with laughter over a joke. What a shame the rest of their day won't be nearly as funny. | You pass through some tall weeds to get a good look at %location%. There are a few peasants walking about, completely oblivious to the cat-like destruction stalking through the grass just outside their little hamlet. Scanning the area, you begin to plot your next move. | %location% is quiet, a little too quiet for a place targeted for destruction. You shake your head at the cruelty of this world, but then remind yourself that this is a job you're going to be getting well paid for. That makes it a little easier. | Killing peasants was never really your forte. Not that you couldn't do it, but the simplicity of it always rubbed you the wrong way. Like killing a legless dog, or stepping on a blind frog. But nobody ever paid you much to put a mutt to sleep. How ironic that these peasants would have been safer as mongrels than humans.\x7d"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_16.png[/img]\x7bLlegas al %location%. Los campesinos están por ahí, justo como imaginabas. Ahora, la pregunta es: ¿cómo quieres abordarlo? | El %location% es un poco más tranquilo de lo que esperabas. Algunos campesinos deambulan por allí, lanzando hoces y azadas mientras charlan sobre esto o aquello. Los escuchas riendo a carcajadas por un chiste. Qué lástima que el resto de su día no será ni de lejos tan divertido. | Pasas entre algunas hierbas altas para echar un buen vistazo al %location%. Hay algunos campesinos caminando, completamente ajenos a la destrucción sigilosa que se esconde en la hierba justo afuera de su pequeño pueblo. Escaneando la zona, comienzas a planear tu próximo movimiento. | El %location% está tranquilo, un poco demasiado tranquilo para un lugar marcado para la destrucción. Te sacudes la cabeza ante la crueldad de este mundo, pero luego te recuerdas que este es un trabajo por el que te pagarán generosamente. Eso lo hace un poco más fácil. | Matar campesinos nunca fue realmente tu especialidad. No es que no pudieras hacerlo, pero la simplicidad de ello siempre te pareció desagradable. Como matar a un perro sin patas o pisotear una rana ciega. Pero nadie te pagó mucho por poner a dormir a un cachorro. Qué irónico que estos campesinos estarían más seguros como perros callejeros que como seres humanos.\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "Encircle them!"
        es = "¡Rodéenlos!"
    }
    {
        en = "Sweep through from one side!"
        es = "¡Barrédlos desde el flanco!"
    }
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_141.png[/img]\x7bYou reach %location% and immediately tell your men to hold and get down. Peasants are afoot, but so are militia. This was not part of the deal and you must reassess the situation accordingly. | As you near %location%, %randombrother% returns to you with a scouting report. Apparently, there are not just peasants there. A few militiamen are in the area. If you are to do this, you'll have to fight them, too. What now? | Militia! They were not part of the plan at all! If you are to proceed, you'll have to take care of them along with the peasants. Time to think carefully about this... | What is this? You see militiamen marching around %location%. Now you'll have to do some real fighting if you want to complete your task. | As you ready to attack %location%, %randombrother% points out something in the distance. Slimming your eyes, you bring into focus a handful of what look like militiamen. This was not part of the agreement! You can still go through with the attack, but there will be some resistance...\x7d"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_141.png[/img]\x7bAl llegar al %location%, de inmediato ordenas a tus hombres que se detengan y se agachen. Hay campesinos a la vista, pero también milicianos. Esto no estaba en el trato y debes reevaluar la situación en consecuencia. | Mientras te acercas a %location%, %randombrother% vuelve a ti con un informe de reconocimiento. Aparentemente, no solo hay campesinos allí. Algunos milicianos están en la zona. Si planeas hacer esto, tendrás que luchar contra ellos también. ¿Qué harás ahora? | ¡Milicianos! ¡No estaban en el plan en absoluto! Si decides proceder, tendrás que ocuparte de ellos junto con los campesinos. Es hora de pensar cuidadosamente en esto... | ¿Qué es esto? Ves a milicianos patrullando alrededor del %location%. Ahora tendrás que enfrentar una verdadera pelea si deseas completar tu tarea. | Mientras te preparas para atacar %location%, %randombrother% señala algo en la distancia. Entrecerrando los ojos, logras distinguir a un puñado de lo que parecen ser milicianos. ¡Esto no estaba en el acuerdo! Aún puedes llevar a cabo el ataque, pero habrá resistencia...\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img]\x7bThe slaughter was a success. You take torches to the place and leave it in smoldering ruin. | A copper smell lingers in the air as you step over and around the bodies of peasants. You nod at your handiwork then look to %randombrother% and give the order.%SPEECH_ON%Burn it all.%SPEECH_OFF% | They put up a little more of a fight than expected, but ultimately you slayed them all. Or, at least, you hope you did. Not wanting to go half-assed on this, you proceed to set fire to every building in sight. | You've brought ruin to the %location%. Its inhabitants are slain, and its buildings set ablaze. A good day's work by any sellsword's summation. | The dead are everywhere and the fresh, sweet smell of their passing is already turning sour. Not one to linger in a stench, you quickly set the %location% ablaze and depart. | ...and so the 'resistance' is put down. A few bodies here, a few there. You hope you got them all. All that's left to do is burn everything to ashes and make your leave. | Well, this is what you came here for. You have a few men display the dead bodies in a manner that you find 'informative', and then have a few other sellswords take torches to every building in sight.\x7d"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_02.png[/img]\x7bLa masacre fue un éxito. Llevas antorchas al lugar y lo dejas en ruinas humeantes. | Un olor a cobre impregna el aire mientras pasas por encima y alrededor de los cuerpos de los campesinos. Asientes ante tu obra y luego miras a %randombrother% y das la orden.%SPEECH_ON%Quémalo todo.%SPEECH_OFF% | Ofrecieron más resistencia de la esperada, pero al final los mataste a todos. O al menos eso esperas. Sin querer hacer las cosas a medias, procedes a prender fuego a todos los edificios a la vista. | Has traído la ruina al %location%. Sus habitantes están muertos y sus edificios en llamas. Un buen día de trabajo según la valoración de cualquier mercenario. | Los muertos están por todas partes y el olor fresco y dulce de su paso ya se está volviendo agrio. No te gusta quedarte en un hedor, así que rápidamente prendes fuego el %location% y te vas. | ... y así se sofoca la 'resistencia'. Unos cuerpos aquí, otros allá. Esperas haberlos eliminado a todos. Todo lo que queda por hacer es reducir todo a cenizas y marcharte. | Bueno, para esto viniste. Haces que unos cuantos hombres dispongan los cadáveres de una manera que encuentras 'informativa', y luego haces que otros mercenarios prendan fuego a todos los edificios a la vista.\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "We're done here."
        es = "Hemos terminado aquí."
    }
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_78.png[/img]\x7bYou get to the %location% only to be greeted by a heavily armed group of men. One of them steps forward, his thumbs hooked into a belt holding up a sword.%SPEECH_ON%Well, well, you really are stupid. %employer% does not forget easily - and he hasn't forgotten the last time you betrayed %faction%. Consider this a little... return of the favor.%SPEECH_OFF%Suddenly, all the men behind the lieutenant charge forward. Arm yourselves, this was an ambush! | You walk into the %location%, but the villagers seem prepared: you see windows shuttering and doors clapping closed. Just as you are about to order the company to start the slaughter, a group of men walk out from behind a building.\n\nThey are... considerably more armed than a group of laymen. In fact, they're carrying %employer%'s banner. The realization that you've been set up dawns on you just as the men begin to charge and you quickly bark out an order for the men to arm themselves. | A man greets you on the road just outside the %location%. He's well armed, well armored, and apparently quite happy, grinning sheepishly as you approach.%SPEECH_ON%Evening, mercenaries. %employer% sends his regards.%SPEECH_OFF%Just then, a group of men swarm out from the sides of the road. It's an ambush! That damned nobleman has betrayed you! | You step foot in the %location%, but all there is to greet you is a gust of lonely wind groaning between old woodworks. Thinking you've been had, you draw out your sword.%SPEECH_ON%Good thinking.%SPEECH_OFF%The voice comes from a building, out stepping a man with his own hand unsheathing a blade. A retinue of armed men wearing the colors of %faction% follow behind him in lockstep, their group fanning out to stare at your company.%SPEECH_ON%I'm going to enjoy prying that sword from your cold grip.%SPEECH_OFF%You shrug and ask why you've been setup.%SPEECH_ON%%employer% doesn't forget those who doublecross him or his house. That's about all you need to know. Not like anything I say here will do you good when you're dead.%SPEECH_OFF%To arms, then, for this is an ambush! | The %location% is empty. Your men scour the buildings and find not a soul. Suddenly, a few men crowd the road behind you, the lieutenant of the group walking forward with ill intent. He's got a cloth embroidered with %employer%'s sigil.%SPEECH_ON%Awfully quiet, isn't it? If you're wondering why I'm here, it is to pay a debt owed to %faction%. You promised a task well done. You could not own up to that promise. Now you die.%SPEECH_OFF%You unsheathe your sword and flash its blade at the lieutenant.%SPEECH_ON%Looks like %faction% is about to have another promise broken.%SPEECH_OFF%\x7d"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_78.png[/img]\x7bLlegas a %location% solo para ser recibido por un grupo de hombres fuertemente armados. Uno de ellos da un paso adelante, con los pulgares enganchados en un cinturón que sostiene una espada.%SPEECH_ON%Bien, bien, eres realmente estúpido. El %employer% no olvida fácilmente, y no ha olvidado la última vez que traicionaste a la %faction%. Considera esto como una pequeña... devolución del favores.%SPEECH_OFF%De repente, todos los hombres detrás del teniente avanzan hacia ti rápidamente. ¡Prepara tus armas, esto fue una emboscada todo el tiempo! | Entras en %location%, pero los aldeanos parecen estar preparados: ves ventanas cerrándose y puertas golpeando al cerrarse. Justo cuando estás a punto de ordenar a la compañía que comience la masacre, un grupo de hombres sale de detrás de un edificio.\n\nEstán... considerablemente mejor armados que un grupo de personas comunes. De hecho, están llevando la bandera del %employer%. Te das cuenta de que te han tendido una trampa justo cuando los hombres comienzan a cargar, y rápidamente ordenas a tus hombres que desenvainen y se preparen para la batala. | Un hombre te saluda en el camino justo afuera del %location%. Está bien armado, bien protegido y aparentemente muy feliz, sonriendo tímidamente mientras te acercas.%SPEECH_ON%Buenas tardes, mercenarios. %employer% envía sus saludos.%SPEECH_OFF%De repente, un grupo de hombres emerge de los lados del camino. ¡Es una emboscada! ¡Ese maldito noble te ha traicionado! | Pisas el %location%, pero lo único que te saluda es una ráfaga de viento solitario gimiendo entre las viejas estructuras de madera. Pensando que te han engañado, desenvainas tu espada.%SPEECH_ON%Buena idea.%SPEECH_OFF%La voz proviene de un edificio, donde sale un hombre acorazado con su propia espada desenvainada. Un séquito de hombres armados vestidos con los colores de la %faction% lo sigue a paso firme, su grupo se expande para observar a tu compañía.%SPEECH_ON%Voy a disfrutar quitándote esa espada de las manos frías.%SPEECH_OFF%Encoges los hombros y preguntas por qué te han tendido una trampa.%SPEECH_ON%El %employer% no olvida a quienes lo traicionan a él o a su casa. Eso es todo lo que necesitas saber. No es como si lo que diga aquí te servirá de mucho cuando estés muerto.%SPEECH_OFF%¡A las armas, entonces, porque esto es una emboscada! | %location% está vacío. Tus hombres exploran los edificios y no encuentran a nadie. De repente, unos hombres se amontonan en el camino detrás de ti, y el teniente del grupo avanza con malas intenciones. Lleva un tabardo bordado con el emblema del %employer%.%SPEECH_ON%Muy tranquilo, ¿verdad? Si te preguntas por qué estoy aquí, es para cobrar una deuda pendiente con %faction%. Prometiste un trabajo bien hecho. No pudiste cumplir esa promesa. Ahora, le prometí al %employer% tu cabeza.%SPEECH_OFF%Desenvainas tu espada y haces brillar su hoja ante el teniente.%SPEECH_ON%Parece que los %faction% están a punto de ver otra promesa rota.%SPEECH_OFF%\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "Damn them!"
        es = "¡Que les den!"
    }
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_61.png[/img]\x7bYou return to %employer% and tell him the news. He sits back and nods.%SPEECH_ON%All of them?%SPEECH_OFF%You look around.%SPEECH_ON%You heard anybody come by?%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% smiles and shakes his head.%SPEECH_ON%Only news of some terrible event, of course. Damned brigands.%SPEECH_OFF%He snaps his fingers and a man seemingly steps out of the darkness to pay you your reward. | %employer% welcomes your return, giving you a drink. He smiles warmly for a man who has just ordered the slaughter of peasants.%SPEECH_ON%I hear news on the wind that %location% has been brought to ruin.%SPEECH_OFF%You nod.%SPEECH_ON%Brigands, huh?%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% grins. He hands you a satchel of crowns.%SPEECH_ON%Brigands indeed.%SPEECH_OFF% | With %location% destroyed, you return to tell %employer% of the news. There's a few locals standing alongside him, so you turn the 'news' that 'brigands' have attacked the place. He nods, concerned, but with a slick sleight of hand slips you a satchel of crowns. He then turns to the locals and says something must be done about a brigand problem... | You tell %employer% of your successes. He smiles and then calls a crowd of commoners to him. He announces that 'brigands' have destroyed %location% and that he'll have to raise taxes to take care of this newfound problem. When he's finished talking, he turns and slides a satchel of crowns into your coat. | You enter %employer%'s abode. There's a woman by his side sobbing. When you look at him, he shakes his head. Nodding, you tell him of the 'news.'%SPEECH_ON%Uh... brigands... have destroyed %location%.%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% nods solemnly.%SPEECH_ON%Yes, yes I know. The widow here has told me everything. Tragic news. Very tragic.%SPEECH_OFF%One of the man's employees hands you a satchel of crowns as you leave.\x7d"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_61.png[/img]\x7bRegresas con %employer% y le informas de las noticias. Se reclina en su silla y asiente.%SPEECH_ON%¿Todos ellos?%SPEECH_OFF%Miras a tu alrededor.%SPEECH_ON%¿Oíste a alguien pasar por aquí?%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% sonríe y sacude la cabeza.%SPEECH_ON%Solo noticias de un terrible evento, por supuesto. Malditos bandidos.%SPEECH_OFF%Chasquea los dedos y un hombre parece salir de la oscuridad y te paga tu recompensa. | %employer% te recibe a tu regreso y te ofrece una bebida. Sonríe cálidamente para ser un hombre que ordenó el exterminio de campesinos.%SPEECH_ON%El viento trajo noticias de que %location% ha sido dejado en ruinas.%SPEECH_OFF%Asientes.%SPEECH_ON%¿Bandidos, eh?%SPEECH_OFF% %employer% sonríe y te entrega una bolsa pesada de monedas.%SPEECH_ON%Bandidos, sin duda.%SPEECH_OFF% | Con %location% destruido, regresas con %employer% para darle las noticias. Hay algunos lugareños junto a él, así que das la 'noticia' de que 'bandidos' han atacado el lugar. Él asiente preocupado, pero con un hábil truco de manos te desliza una bolsa de coronas. Luego se gira hacia los lugareños y menciona que se debe hacer algo acerca con el problema de bandidos... | Le cuentas a %employer% acerca de tus éxitos. Sonríe y luego llama a una multitud de plebeyos. Anuncia que 'bandidos' han destruido %location% y que tendrá que aumentar los impuestos para cuidar de este nuevo problema. Cuando termina de hablar, se gira y desliza una bolsa de coronas en tu abrigo. | Entras en la morada de %employer%. Hay una mujer a su lado sollozando. Cuando lo miras, él sacude la cabeza. Asientes y le cuentas las 'noticias'. %SPEECH_ON%Ehh... bandidos... han destruido el %location%.%SPEECH_OFF% %employer% asiente solemnemente.%SPEECH_ON%Sí, sí, lo sé. La viuda aquí me ha contado todo. Noticias trágicas. Muy trágicas.%SPEECH_OFF% Uno de los empleados del hombre te entrega una bolsa de coronas mientras te vas.\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "\x7bHonest pay for honest work. | Crowns is crowns.\x7d"
        es = "\x7bPaga honesta para trabajo honesto. | Coronas son coronas.\x7d"
    }
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_61.png[/img]\x7bYou enter %townname% to find a number of familiar peasants standing around %employer%. Fearing they'll recognize you, you stay out of sight. They cry out that brigands have destroyed %location%. %employer% looks concerned.%SPEECH_ON%Have they? Oh, that's awful! I will look into this. Fear not, people, I will protect you!%SPEECH_OFF%Just as the man finishes, one of his guards slips you a satchel of crowns. | You enter %employer%'s abode to find a number of bloodied peasants standing around his desk. You stay hidden as they finish their talk and leave. %employer% waves you in.%SPEECH_ON%Brigands. They said brigands did it. Perfect. Your payment is in the corner.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% greets your return with a smile.%SPEECH_ON%There were survivors.%SPEECH_OFF%He waves off your concern.%SPEECH_ON%They think brigands were responsible. A simple raid by vagabonds. You have nothing to worry about. Your payment...%SPEECH_OFF%He slides a satchel across his desk. You take it and nod.%SPEECH_ON%Good doing business with you.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% slaps a scroll down on his desk as you enter.%SPEECH_ON%You left some of them alive! But... it's alright. They think brigands were responsible.%SPEECH_OFF%You put a hand to your sword's hilt and glance at one of %employer%'s guards.%SPEECH_ON%I still expect to be paid in full.%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% waves his hand to his desk where a satchel is.%SPEECH_ON%Of course. But next time I ask you to do something, I expect you to do it in full, understand?%SPEECH_OFF% | A throng of peasants have circled %employer%. You briefly wonder if they are about to lynch the man, but instead he sends them off. As he watches them turn a corner, he explains that they are survivors from %location%. Before you can say another word, the man waves off your concern.%SPEECH_ON%They still think brigands were responsible, but I'm not happy about this result. This could have gone very bad for us. For me, I mean.%SPEECH_OFF%You nod and ask if you want these few survivors killed, just to be sure. %employer% shakes his head.%SPEECH_ON%No, no need for that. Here is your payment as promised, sellsword. Next time, though, do be sure to follow my orders.%SPEECH_OFF%\x7d"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_61.png[/img]\x7bEntras en %townname% y ves a un grupo de campesinos conocidos reunidos alrededor de %employer%. Temiendo que te reconozcan, te mantienes fuera de su vista. Gritan que los bandidos han destruido %location%. %employer% parece preocupado.%SPEECH_ON%¿Lo han hecho? ¡Oh, eso es terrible! Investigaré esto. ¡No teman, gente, los protegeré!%SPEECH_OFF%Justo cuando el hombre termina, uno de sus guardias te entrega una bolsa de coronas. | Entras en la morada de %employer% para encontrar a un grupo de campesinos ensangrentados junto a su escritorio. Te mantienes oculto mientras terminan su conversación y se van. %employer% te hace un gesto para que te acerques.%SPEECH_ON%Bandidos. Dicen que fueron los bandidos. Perfecto. Tu pago está en la esquina.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% te saluda a tu regreso con una sonrisa.%SPEECH_ON%Había supervivientes.%SPEECH_OFF%Olas tu preocupación te azotan.%SPEECH_ON%Piensan que los culpables fueron bandidos. Un simple ataque de malandros. No tienes de qué preocuparte. Tu pago...%SPEECH_OFF%Desliza una bolsa a través de su escritorio. La tomas y asientes.%SPEECH_ON%Es un placer hacer negocios contigo.%SPEECH_OFF% | %employer% golpea un pergamino en su escritorio cuando entras.%SPEECH_ON%¡Dejaste a algunos con vida! Pero... está bien. Piensan que fueron los bandidos.%SPEECH_OFF%Recuestas tu mano en el pomo de tu espada y miras a uno de los guardias de %employer%.%SPEECH_ON%Aún espero que me paguen en su totalidad.%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% mueve la mano hacia su escritorio donde hay una bolsa.%SPEECH_ON%Por supuesto. Pero la próxima vez que te pida que hagas algo, espero que lo hagas en su totalidad, ¿entendido?%SPEECH_OFF% | Una multitud de campesinos ha rodeado a %employer%. Te preguntas brevemente si están a punto de linchar al hombre, pero en cambio los despide. Mientras los observa doblar una esquina, explica que son supervivientes del %location%. Antes de que puedas decir otra palabra, %employer% desestima tu preocupación.%SPEECH_ON%Aún piensan que fueron los bandidos, pero no estoy contento con este resultado. Esto podría haber salido muy mal para nosotros. Quiero decir, para mí.%SPEECH_OFF%Asientes y le preguntas si quiere que se mate a estos pocos supervivientes, solo para estar seguro. %employer% niega con la cabeza.%SPEECH_ON%No, no es necesario. Aquí tienes tu pago como se prometió, mercenario. La próxima vez, asegúrate de seguir mis órdenes.%SPEECH_OFF%\x7d"
    }
    {
        // this.World.FactionManager.getFaction(this.Contract.getFaction()).addPlayerRelation(this.Const.World.Assets.RelationNobleContractPoor, "Fulfilled a contract");
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "<this.World.FactionManager.getFaction(this.m.Faction).addPlayerRelation(this.Const.World.Assets.RelationContractCancel, Broke a contract)>"
        es = "<this.World.FactionManager.getFaction(this.m.Faction).addPlayerRelation(this.Const.World.Assets.RelationContractCancel, Romper un contrato)>"
    }
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_43.png[/img]\x7bAs you enter %employer%'s abode he turns and slaps a scroll of a drawing on his table.%SPEECH_ON%Recognize this person?%SPEECH_OFF%You pick it up. The sketched face looks remarkably like your own. %employer% leans back.%SPEECH_ON%They know someone hired a hit on the place. Get the fark out of here before I have my men run you through.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_ON%Survivors! Survivors! What did I say, 'no survivors', I believe I said that, right?%SPEECH_OFF%You nod as %employer% curls his knuckles against his desk.%SPEECH_ON%So why in the hell do I get peasants running in here crying that mercenaries stormed their place? Dead people don't talk, but who does? Who talks, sellsword?%SPEECH_OFF%You stand.%SPEECH_ON%Survivors.%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% points toward the door.%SPEECH_ON%Right. Now get the hell out of my sight.%SPEECH_OFF% | You nod as %employer% tells you the news: a few peasants escaped and spread word that it was a 'hired job' to destroy %location%. But you're wondering...%SPEECH_ON%Can we still keep all the equipment we've found?%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% laughs.%SPEECH_ON%You can keep whatever the hell you like, but you won't be seeing a single crown out of my pockets. Get out of here, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF% | Unfortunately, it appears that a few peasants survived the slaughter. They told %employer% of very particular details, namely that well-armed and ill-intentioned men destroyed %location%. Not brigands, but sellswords. You were supposed to kill them all, leaving no survivors, but now... well, now you don't get paid. | %employer% sits across from you, clenching his fist, his face growing red. He asks how he is to raise taxes to protect people from brigands if everyone thinks mercenaries were hired to destroy %location%. You inquire as to what he means and the man is very blunt with you: a few peasants survived, you farkin' idiot. Leaving survivors was not part of the job description, it appears, and now %employer%'s payment won't be a part of your treasury.\x7d"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_43.png[/img]\x7bAl entrar en la residencia de %employer%, este te muestra un dibujo.%SPEECH_ON%¿Reconoces a esta persona?%SPEECH_OFF% Tienes en tus manos el dibujo de un rostro que se parece notablemente al tuyo. %employer% se recuesta y continúa.%SPEECH_ON%Saben que alguien contrató un ataque al lugar. Lárgate de aquí antes de que haga que mis hombres te atraviesen con una lanza.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_ON%¡Supervivientes! ¡SUPERVIVIENTES! \x22Ningún sobreviviente\x22, creo que dije eso, ¿verdad?%SPEECH_OFF% Asientes mientras %employer% aprieta los puños contra su escritorio. %SPEECH_ON%Entonces, ¿por qué diablos tengo campesinos entrando aquí llorando que mercenarios asaltaron su lugar? La gente muerta no habla, pero ¿quién lo hace? ¿Quién habla, mercenario?%SPEECH_OFF% Te pones de pie. %SPEECH_ON%Supervivientes.%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% señala hacia la puerta. %SPEECH_ON%Correcto. Ahora lárgate de mi vista.%SPEECH_OFF% | Asientes mientras %employer% te da las noticias: algunos campesinos escaparon y difundieron la noticia de que se trataba de un \x22trabajo contratado\x22 para destruir el %location%. Pero te preguntas...%SPEECH_ON%¿Podemos quedarnos con el equipo que encontramos?%SPEECH_OFF%%employer% se ríe. %SPEECH_ON%Puedes quedarte con lo que quieras, pero no verás ni una sola moneda de mis bolsillos. Lárgate de aquí, mercenario.%SPEECH_OFF% | Desafortunadamente, parece que algunos campesinos sobrevivieron a la masacre. Informaron a %employer% sobre detalles muy específicos, a saber, que hombres bien armados y con malas intenciones destruyeron %location%. No fueron bandidos, sino mercenarios. Supuestamente, debías matarlos a todos, sin dejar sobrevivientes, pero ahora... bueno, ahora no recibirás tu pago. | %employer% está sentado frente a ti, apretando el puño, su rostro se torna rojo. Te pregunta cómo hará para aumentar los impuestos y proteger a la gente de los bandidos si todos piensan que se contrató a mercenarios para destruir el %location%. Tú preguntas a qué se refiere y el hombre es muy franco contigo: unos cuantos campesinos sobrevivieron, maldito idiota. Dejar sobrevivientes no era parte de la descripción del trabajo, al parecer, y ahora el pago de %employer% no formará parte de tu tesorería."
    }
    {
        // Text = "They won\'t be welcoming us in %settlementname%...",
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "They won't be welcoming us in %settlementname%..."
        es = "No nos recibirán muy bien en %settlementname%..."
    }
    {
        // this.Contract.m.Destination.getSettlement().getFactionOfType(this.Const.FactionType.Settlement).addPlayerRelation(this.Const.World.Assets.RelationAttacked, "Raided " + this.Flags.get("DestinationName"));
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "<this.World.FactionManager.getFaction(this.m.Faction).addPlayerRelation(this.Const.World.Assets.RelationContractCancel, Broke a contract)>"
        es = "<this.World.FactionManager.getFaction(this.m.Faction).addPlayerRelation(this.Const.World.Assets.RelationContractCancel, Romper un contrato)>"
    }
    {
        en = "settlementname"
        es = ""
    }
    // FILE: D:\GOG\Battle Brothers\!Downloads\bbros\bin\comparer\original_current\scripts\contracts\contracts\restore_location_contract.nut
    {
        en = "Rebuilding Effort"
        es = "Labor de reconstrucción"
    }
